    "https://www.marian.edu/human-resources/index.php": {
      "title": "Popular Searches",
      "description": "Human Resources | Marian University Skip To Top Navigation Skip To Content Skip To Footer Open Menu Apply Visit Give myMU About Marian Our Story Campus Tour Why Choose Marian? Meet Our Leaders Mission & Values Franciscan Values Art Walks on Campus Academics Explore All Majors Schools and Programs St. Joe's (Earn and Learn) Nashville (Nursing Program) Academic Calendar Study Abroad Online Admissions Start Your Application Connect with Your Counselor Tuition Costs Financial Aid Scholarships Athletics Join the Marian Knights Join the Ancilla Chargers Experience Campus Student Clubs Campus Housing Campus Safety Faith Activities Student Support Latest News University News Student Success Campus Events University Blog Research Engage in Research Join Funded Projects Conduct Undergraduate Research About You Future Student Current Student Faculty or Staff Parent or Family Alumni Locations Indianapolis Campus Plymouth Resource Links Directory MUHub Portal Connect Outlook Email Marketing Request Canvas Registrar Maintenance Request IT Helpdesk Close Apply Visit Give myMU Search Close Search Popular Searches Degrees and Programs Financial Aid and Scholarships Campus Tours Housing Careers at Marian Maps and Directions Close Human Resources Browse Section Why Indy? From cool cultural districts with unique entertainment, shopping, and dining options to outdoor festivals, professional and amateur sports events, hiking and biking trails, and more, Marian University is conveniently located in the heart of it all. Explore CAREERS at Marian Indy is a TechHub Marian is located just 5 miles away from downtown Indy. Arts and Culture Catch a show, visit a gallery, or create something yourself. Family Friendly In Indy, you have the chance to learn, play, and grow as a family. Active Lifestyle Stay active with Indy’s various sports and recreation. Marian University feels different—in the best way. It’s a close-knit community where Franciscan values really guide how we show up for students and for each other. Seeing the impact my work has on students and our community is what gives it meaning, and I’m proud to be part of a thriving, visionary university. Tanja Greene, MSBME Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering Benefits The health and financial security of you and your family is important to us. Our benefits program provides a variety of plans that can enhance the lives of you and your family — both now and in the future. Retirement No matter your stage in life, you can plan and save for the retirement you want. We offer a 403(b) plan with a generous match, personalized services, and many investment options. Compliance Marian University is a non-Grandfathered Plan and meets both the minimum essential coverage and values as defined by the Affordable Care Act. Medical You are covered at the highest level with one of the biggest networks through United Health Care – Surest. Disability This plan provides income protection while you are off work due to sickness or disability. This benefit is 100% employer paid. Voluntary Vision With an EyeMed provider, you will receive discounts for services provided and the plan will reimburse the maximum allowable benefits. Life/AD&D This plan provides Life and AD&D benefits for all full-time employees. This benefit is 100% employer paid. Voluntary Dental You will receive the highest benefits when you use a Provider in the Sun Life Dental. Voluntary Life and AD&D You can purchase life and AD&D insurance for you and eligible dependents at a small cost. Request Information Reach Out to Us Marian University 3200 Cold Spring Road Indianapolis, IN 46222-1997 (317) 955-6000 admissions@marian.edu (Undergrad) COMadmissions@marian.edu (Medical) plymouthadmissions@marian.edu (Plymouth) onlineadmissions@marian.edu (Online) gradmissions@marian.edu (Graduate) Learn More About Marian Get in touch and we'll talk to you soon. #GoKnights⚔️ Undergrad: 4-Year Programs Undergrad: Plymouth Location Undergrad: 2-Year Saint Joe Indy Undergrad: Online Programs Graduate Programs Medical School Non-Degree Options K-12 Online Program Explore Our Programs Arts & Sciences Business Community & Health Sciences Education Engineering Nursing Online Osteopathic Medicine St. Joe's (Earn and Learn) Student Resources Accessibility Services Consumer Information CORE Job Opportunities Privacy Policy Report Bias/Misconduct Report Fraud/Abuse Research Oversight Title IX Support Our Locations Indianapolis Campus Plymouth Campus Services All Departments A - Z Advancement Billing & Payments Campus Safety Careers at Marian Conferences and Events Health and Wellness Marketing Support Tech Support University Libraries Start Your Journey Apply as an Undergrad Apply as a Grad Student Apply as a K-12 Student Financial Aid Experience Marian Visit Campus Campus Map Faculty Directory Why Marian? Latest News Apply Now Schedule a Tour Give to Marian Work at Marian © 2026 Marian University Notice of Nondiscrimination: Marian University does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, creed, national origin, age or disabilities in the selection of administrative personnel, faculty and staff, and students. Placement rates are gathered from data collected from graduates within six months of graduation. Students may make a complaint to the Indiana Commission of Higher Education. Marian University was founded by the Sisters of St. Francis of Oldenburg, Indiana, and continues its Catholic Franciscan mission through sponsorship by the Third Order Franciscan University Alliance."
